<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany's Chancellor Merz fighting for political survival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:682bd89c9f4b808c432f4d712c00dd634aadddf2c125c8623090b067334786d5</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-chancellor-merz-fighting-for-political-survival/a-79290192--4c7403d99c36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-chancellor-merz-fighting-for-political-survival/a-79290192?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the CDU's crushing defeat in the Saxony-Anhalt state election, many are expressing doubts about their party leader, Chancellor Friedrich Merz. But they don't appear to have any viable alternative.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz to cancel UN trip amid party infighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae908fbc286bcc3a1624d7eb14693cce07d58426175e79a3ac1b7f92f9d3a645</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:34:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-to-cancel-un-trip-over-party-infighting/live-79273324--971a6ac4ea62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-to-cancel-un-trip-amid-party-infighting/live-79273324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's chancellor nixxed his trip over doubts about his leadership after party losses to the AfD in state elections. Meanwhile, Defense Minister Pistorius is in Washington for talks with his US counterpart.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz urges CDU discipline as pressure grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9d64ed94cd3e9c761f1b346778636763ff4e30193e20ba9b4dda1459faefa13</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:34:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T00:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-urges-cdu-discipline-as-pressure-grows/live-79256902--10c6578e951f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-urges-cdu-discipline-as-pressure-grows/live-79256902?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has urged his party to stay disciplined as pressure grows over his leadership. Meanwhile, Germany's homeownership rate has fallen to its lowest level in 20 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German drama 'Blindspot Berlin' revisits 2016 Christmas market attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f1b222ffff1c89e5c21bfa26068d71dd4c2f3b181d51ba31cdcbffcf6d9fa4f</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162--11e3e3b69ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the terrorist attack on a Berlin Christmas market, a new German miniseries looks into the institutional failures that allowed the deadly truck rampage to happen.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Drivers in Germany fume over soaring fuel prices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a23a45c1a7548e19eeb823d39974b8e23e2c05c97642afa0af160148b8ac7220</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/drivers-in-germany-fume-over-soaring-fuel-prices/a-79282456--6a933389e322.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/drivers-in-germany-fume-over-soaring-fuel-prices/a-79282456?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz wants to provide relief to motorists. But exactly how this is to happen remains unclear.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Holocaust survivor on 'very dangerous' AfD Saxony-Anhalt win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf83139c54b0c83d756860740f8689276d156d8360f770b9a68acff6ce45f234</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/holocaust-survivor-on-very-dangerous-afd-saxony-anhalt-win/a-79278429--2441e4b64e9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/holocaust-survivor-on-very-dangerous-afd-saxony-anhalt-win/a-79278429?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Charlotte Knobloch survived the Holocaust by passing as the daughter of non-Jewish farmers. She recently spoke with DW to express her shock following the AfD victory in Saxony-Anhalt's state election.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Socialist Left leads far-right AfD ahead of Berlin vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:505df8f5d45f6f88ff7cb1a54a90a0c4135b48bc436acc52efbc3488abad69e4</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:34:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/socialist-left-leads-far-right-afd-ahead-of-berlin-vote/a-79256516--23dd67cf573c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/socialist-left-leads-far-right-afd-ahead-of-berlin-vote/a-79256516?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The results of the Berlin election are as hard to predict as ever. Three parties are vying for first place, including the socialist Left Party and the far-right AfD. But one issue is most important to Berliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:34:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-16T13:34:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
